 search\nL20: \nL21: ChEBI ID  | CHEBI:32150\nL22: ChEBI Name  | sodium thiosulfate pentahydrate\nL23: Stars  |\nL24: Definition  | A hydrate consisting of sodium thiosulfate with 5 mol eq. of water.\nL25: Last Modified  | 17 May 2024\nL26: Downloads  | 【14†Molfile】\nL27: \nL28: On this page\nL29: \nL30:   * 【15†Intro】\nL31:   * 【16†Roles Classification】\nL32:   * 【17†Ontology】\nL33:   * 【18†Names】\nL34:   * 【19†Manual Xrefs】\nL35:   * 【20†Citations】\nL36: Formula  | 5H2O.2Na.O3S2\nL37: Net Charge  | 0\nL38: Average Mass  | 248.186\nL39: Monoisotopic Mass  | 247.96125\nL40: SMILES  | O=S(=O)([O-])[S-].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[H]O[H].[Na+].[Na+]\nL41: InChI  | InChI=1S/2Na.H2O3S2.5H2O/c;;1-5(2,3)4;;;;;/h;;(H2,1,2,3,4);5*1H2/q2*+1;;;;;;/p-2\nL42: InChIKey  | PODWXQQNRWNDGD-UHFFFAOYSA-L\nL43: \nL44: Roles Classification\nL45: ---\nL46: 【21†Biological Role:】  | 【22†antifungal drug】  Any antifungal agent used to prevent or treat fungal infections in humans or animals.\nL47: 【23†Applications:】  | 【24†nephroprotective agent】  Any protective agent that is able to prevent damage to the kidney.【25†antidote to cyanide poisoning】  A role borne by a molecule that acts to counteract or neutralize the deleterious effects of cyanide.【22†antifungal drug】  Any antifungal agent used to prevent or treat fungal infections in humans or animals.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntris (CHEBI:9754) (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A9754 ; rewritten summary of https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:9754)\nciteturn16view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:9754\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:9754; Total lines: 117\nL0:   * 【0†Advanced Search】\nL1:   * 【1†Submit】\nL2:   * 【2†Downloads】\nL3:   * 【3†Tools】\nL4:   * 【4†Docs】\nL5:   * 【5†About】\nL6:   * 【6†Contact】\nL7: \nL8: 【7†EMBL-EBI†ebi.ac.uk】 | 【8†Chemical Biology Resources】 | 【9†ChEBI】\nL9: \nL10: Search[Input: Enter your search term]\nL11: \nL12: Search\nL13: \nL14: Example searches: 【10†iron*】, 【11†InChI=1S/CH4O/c1-2/h2H,1H3】, 【12†caffeine】 | 【0†Advanced Search】\nL15: ## CHEBI:9754 - tris\nL16: \nL17: 【13†Image: Default Structure】\nL18: \nL19: Take structure to advanced search\nL20: \nL21: ChEBI ID  | CHEBI:9754\nL22: ChEBI Name  | tris\nL23: Stars  |\nL24: Definition  | A primary amino compound that is tert-butylamine in which one hydrogen attached to each methyl group is replaced by a hydroxy group. A compound widely used as a biological buffer substance in the pH range 7—9; pK_{a} = 8.3 at 20 °C; pK_{a} = 7.82 at 37 °C.\nL25: Last Modified  | 22 February 2017\nL26: Downloads  | 【14†Molfile】\nL27: \nL28: On this page\nL29:   * 【15†Intro】\nL30:   * 【16†Roles Classification】\nL31:   * 【17†Ontology】\nL32:   * 【18†Names】\nL33:   * 【19†Manual Xrefs】\nL34:   * 【20†Registry Numbers】\nL35:   * 【21†Citations】\nL36: \nL37: Formula  | C4H11NO3\nL38: Net Charge  | 0\nL39: Average Mass  | 121.136\nL40: Monoisotopic Mass  | 121.07389\nL41: SMILES  | NC(CO)(CO)CO\nL42: InChI  | InChI=1S/C4H11NO3/c5-4(1-6,2-7)3-8/h6-8H,1-3,5H2\nL43: InChIKey  | LENZDBCJOHFCAS-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL44: \nL45: Wikipedia\nL46: ---\nL47: \nL48: Roles Classification\nL49: ---\nL50: 【22†Chemical Roles:】  | 【23†buffer】  Any substance or mixture of substances that, in solution (typically aqueous), resists change in pH upon addition of small amounts of acid or base.【24†Bronsted base】  A molecular entity capable of accepting a hydron from a donor (Brønsted acid).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndiammonium hydrogen phosphate (CHEBI:63051) (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A63051 ; rewritten summary of https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:63051)\nciteturn16view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:63051\",\"lineno\":null}); Red